      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e well, n isn\u0027t a power of 2 (log2(buckets[j])). Simply counting zeros loses too much precision (we end up underestimating the entropy by quite a bit)\n\n?? I think the formula above is correct for any integer n not only power of 2.\nIt\u0027s true though the rounding might not be optimal (it\u0027s always rounding by default), ie\nfloor(log2(n)) \u003d 31 - __builtin_clz(n)\nceil(log2(n)) \u003d 32 - __builtin_clz(n - 1) \n\nso the average of those 2 gives you the closest rounding.",
